                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l36" HPOS="664" VPOS="2536" WIDTH="1664" HEIGHT="49" BASELINE="666 2567 2328 2560" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="666 2567 666 2581 2313 2585 2315 2585 2317 2585 2319 2585 2328 2575 2328 2560 2323 2536 664 2542 666 2567"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="¹ These sounds are represented as long, wailing, monotonous. They are intended to characterize the"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l37" HPOS="559" VPOS="2581" WIDTH="1767" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="561 2610 2326 2606" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="561 2610 561 2624 2323 2628 2326 2606 2321 2581 559 2583 561 2610"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="manner of singing of the white people. The Chukchee manner of singing is different, and consists of short,"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l38" HPOS="561" VPOS="2622" WIDTH="1764" HEIGHT="49" BASELINE="563 2653 2325 2645" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="563 2653 563 2671 2323 2665 2325 2645 2319 2622 561 2628 563 2653"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="rolling, trembling, ever-changing sounds of guttural character. The Chukchee often say that the white people"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l39" HPOS="559" VPOS="2669" WIDTH="306" HEIGHT="41" BASELINE="561 2696 865 2692" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="561 2696 561 2710 865 2708 865 2692 859 2669 559 2671 561 2696"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="sing as dogs howl."/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l40" HPOS="672" VPOS="2708" WIDTH="1654" HEIGHT="45" BASELINE="672 2733 2326 2733" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="672 2733 672 2753 2326 2753 2326 2733 2326 2708 672 2708 672 2733"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="² Greenland tradition also mentions erkigdlit, fabulous and hostile inlanders with faces like those of dogs."/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l41" HPOS="561" VPOS="2747" WIDTH="1764" HEIGHT="48" BASELINE="563 2780 2325 2772" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="563 2780 563 2795 2323 2793 2325 2772 2319 2747 561 2753 563 2780"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="Dall, Murdoch, and others translate this name as “children of a louse’s egg” (Murdoch, Point Barrow Eskimo,"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l42" HPOS="565" VPOS="2786" WIDTH="1761" HEIGHT="58" BASELINE="567 2827 2326 2817" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="567 2827 567 2844 2325 2830 2326 2817 2323 2792 1276 2786 1274 2786 1272 2786 1243 2795 956 2788 954 2788 565 2799 567 2827"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="p. 51). The Reindeer Chukchee call the Maritime dog-breeders, in a somewhat similar way, “born from dog-"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l43" HPOS="561" VPOS="2832" WIDTH="189" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="561 2864 750 2864" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="561 2864 561 2879 750 2879 750 2864 748 2832 561 2836 561 2864"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="excrement.”"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l44" HPOS="672" VPOS="2873" WIDTH="1656" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="674 2905 2328 2899" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="674 2905 674 2920 2328 2914 2328 2899 2323 2873 672 2877 674 2905"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="³ Argentoff mentions the name Pavluchka as used in Chukchee traditions. I could not find this mentioned,"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l45" HPOS="559" VPOS="2916" WIDTH="1764" HEIGHT="49" BASELINE="561 2947 2323 2940" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="561 2947 561 2965 2321 2959 2323 2940 2317 2916 559 2922 561 2947"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="in the papers of Argentoff, but have met with it in an article in a Russian review, that related to one of my"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l46" HPOS="561" VPOS="2955" WIDTH="1764" HEIGHT="49" BASELINE="563 2988 2325 2984" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="563 2988 563 3004 2323 3002 2325 2984 2319 2955 561 2963 563 2988"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="own papers. The article mentions that the paper by Argentoff in question here is very rare, and has appeared"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l47" HPOS="559" VPOS="3002" WIDTH="1764" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="561 3031 2323 3025" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="2317 3002 559 3006 561 3031 561 3049 2323 3049 2323 3025 2321 3018 2317 3002"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="in Siberia. I have not come across the name Pavluchka in Chukchee stories and traditions. The Chukchee,"/>
                    </TextLine>

                    <TextLine ID="mz_3-118_l48" HPOS="561" VPOS="3045" WIDTH="1432" HEIGHT="47" BASELINE="563 3076 1993 3068" TAGREFS="TYPE_5">
                        <Shape>
                            <Polygon POINTS="563 3076 563 3092 1993 3088 1993 3068 1987 3045 561 3051 563 3076"/>
                        </Shape>
                        <String CONTENT="upon the whole, are inclined to substitute for alien names new compositions of their own."/>
                    </TextLine>
